Biscuit-dough NIR spectra
=========================

Source
------
The ``cookie`` data set of the R package ppls 2.0.0 (CRAN), file data/cookie.rda.
The R packages groc 1.0.10 and seedCCA 3.1 (CRAN) carry the same values.

References
----------
Osborne, B. G., Fearn, T., Miller, A. R. and Douglas, S. *Application of near infrared
reflectance spectroscopy to the compositional analysis of biscuits and biscuit doughs.*
Journal of the Science of Food and Agriculture, 35(1), 99-105 (1984).
https://doi.org/10.1002/jsfa.2740350116

Brown, P. J., Fearn, T. and Vannucci, M. *Bayesian wavelet regression on curves with
application to a spectroscopic calibration problem.* Journal of the American Statistical
Association, 96(454), 398-408 (2001). https://doi.org/10.1198/016214501753168118

Contents
--------
biscuit.csv: 72 unbaked biscuit doughs, one row each. ``sample`` numbers them 1 to 72 in
the upstream order; ``set`` is ``calibration`` for the first 40 and ``validation`` for the
other 32; ``fat``, ``sucrose``, ``dry_flour`` and ``water`` are the percentages of each
ingredient; the 700 columns ``1100`` to ``2498`` are the NIR reflectance spectrum, one
column per wavelength in nm, at 2 nm intervals. The values are the upstream values,
unchanged; only the column names of the spectrum are the wavelengths instead of 1 to 700.

